    <Documents>
        <Document ID="2DFE9CFF-07B9-49E5-A0CA-AF23DBB63535">
            <Title>Process</Title>
            <Text>This is a KATA. It’s not a real project. 
Hence, by definition there’ll be (unrealistic) simplifications and a smoothing out of the problem space. The sharp edges of reality are extracted so we can focus on the crux of the topic or the areas we want to practice and improve on. This doesn’t mean it can’t be useful, or interesting!

The topics I personally want to exercise in this Kata are:
	•	ADRs: to provide a record and direction
	•	Architectural Characteristics to drive the process
	•	Using Domain Driven Design for analysis
	•	Using AI to help the architectural design
	•	Think about where AI integrates into an architecture
	•	Use Scrivener and Quarto for documentation


</Text>
        </Document>
        <Document ID="B843BFA6-105F-49EA-9CFB-9D7CCD0ECDD4">
            <Title>0: Process and tools</Title>
            <Text>Status: Accepted
Context:
Firstly let’s set the tools, rules, and processes. ADRs, DDD and AI…
Decision:
	•	Will proceed using ADRs
	•	Will use Domain Driven Design as a analyis framework
	•	Will seek AI feedback on each ADR: in a dedicated section
	•	Will use Scrivener to manage  documents, links, research and deliverables.
Considered Options:
	•	Having a structured Approach is sine qua non
Consequences &amp; Trade-offs:
	•	Positive: This will provide a record of decisions and be methodical
	•	Negative: Requires discipline.
</Text>
        </Document>
        <Document ID="6E166A5C-F0A7-4B33-9751-BD511DBF6F55">
            <Title>Metadata</Title>
            <Synopsis>This is the Pandoc metadata and also contains the pandocomatic key to specify which templates to use</Synopsis>
            <Text># Quarto YAML metadata
# IMPORTANT: YAML config files use SPACES for indentation to 
# define structure. Remember: STRAIGHTEN all smart quotes and don't
# capitalise metadata keys, they MUST BE lowercase! 
# Tip: use "Show Invisibles" in Scrivener to see whitespaces.
# 
# Metadata is used to define the options that Quarto/Pandoc
# use when generating the final document. You will need to change
# the location of your bibliography files and change any fonts
# to those present on your system.
#
title: “Architectural Kata 2026”
subtitle: "A stab at architectural thinking in the age of AI "
author: 
  - name: Julian Harley 
    email: julian@example.com
    corresponding: true
keywords: [architecture, kata, AI]
subject: Architectural report
lang: en
date: &lt;$date:YYYY-MM-dd&gt;      # Scrivener placeholder
verbose: true                 # pandoc verbosity
toc: true                     # table of contents
number-sections: true         # numbered headings
crossref:                     # cross-referencing options
  labels: arabic                # (default is arabic)
  subref-labels: alpha A        # (default is alpha a)
  chapters: true                # Numbers depend on the chapter, e.g. 2.1
cap-location: bottom          # where put figure &amp; table captions
link-citations: true          # in-document links to refs
bibliography: ${USERHOME}/.local/share/pandoc/Core.json
csl: ${USERHOME}/.local/share/pandoc/csl/apa.csl
appendix-style: default       # see https://quarto.org/docs/authoring/appendices.html#appendix-style
dpi: 300
format:
  html:
    theme: journal
    title-block-banner: "#BB3333"
    embed-resources: false
    html-math-method: mathjax
    section-divs: true
    linestretch: 1.5
    fig-format: svg
    mainfont: Alegreya       
    monofont: Rec Mono Duotone #
    # Inject some style tweaks into the header
    header-includes: |
      &lt;style&gt;
        p {text-align: justify;}
        tr.odd {background-color: #F1F1F1;}
        caption, figcaption, .column-margin p {font-family: Alegreya Sans, sans-serif !important; text-align: left !important;}
      &lt;/style&gt;
  pdf:
    documentclass: scrbook    # scrbook, scrreport, scrartcl
    classoption: 
      - oneside                # oneside or twoside
    papersize: a4
    geometry:
      #- showframe             # check the layout
      - top=2cm
      - bottom=2cm
      - head=1cm
      - foot=1cm
      - left=2cm
      - marginparwidth=4cm
      - textwidth=12cm
      - marginparsep=1cm
      - bindingoffset=0.5cm
    fontsize: 12pt
    linestretch: 1.5
    latex-clean: true
    keep-tex: true
    mainfont: Georgia         
    sansfont: Helvetica Neue   
    monofont: Menlo
    mathfont:  STIX Two Math  
    linkcolor: Mahogany
    citecolor: Bittersweet
    urlcolor: BrickRed
    #header-includes: |
      #\KOMAoptions{DIV=last}  # force koma layout rather than geometry
  epub:
    html-math-method: katex
    identifier: 45DRE66-YTX
    epub-cover-image: ${USERHOME}/.local/share/pandoc/templates/cover.jpg
    fig-format: png
  docx:
    prefer-html: true          # stops non-HTML format errors 
    reference-doc: ${USERHOME}/.local/share/pandoc/templates/custom.docx # change to your own docx template 
</Text>
