            <Title>Compiler script details</Title>
            <Text>There is a small ruby script that deals with the reformatting from Scrivener to be compatible with Quarto. It allows you to pass a file name and a format, so you can edit the post-processing panel to change the output format (change html to pdf / docx / epub etc.). It is embedded in this project’s Compiler format:

#

The script’s output is redirected &amp;&gt; to a Quarto.log file and this log file will be opened after the compiler finishes so you can check any details or debug any errors…</Text>
        </Document>
        <Document ID="C0115381-CFEA-4D13-BB6A-C990B005A2EC">
            <Title>Review of the Project Scope</Title>
            <Text>The Project involves thinking about an estate that’s seeking a new direction and is looking to a technological solutions to help them plot their new direction. Event Page
Initial discussion of relevant details

 Von Digitalis Estate is made up of:
	•	Currently: 5000 visitors a day: That’s about equal to about a ten visitors a second.
	⁃	This will generate a spike of traffic on open (and perhaps closing time) and a steady stream of telemetry and monitoring throughout the day
	•	Growth plans to 15,000: These are probably wild guesstimates: it would be wise to be able to scale and cope with a good deal more:  Retaining the ability for x10 capacity increase would be wise. And given the uncertainty, new projects will likely to also be accommodated.

‘Predictions are hard, especially about the future’ Niels Bohr

	•	There’s several broad themes in several domains:
	⁃	Tickets and passes
	⁃	Visitor activity tracking and sensors: for trends and strategic planning
	⁃	Asset telemetry: track activities, health and behaviour of the 40 amusement rides &amp; 200 animals/plants/fish enclosures
</Text>
        </Document>
